{:edb/db-before-t 1278 :edb/db-after-t 1279 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534591 50 #inst "2026-10-08T01:50:56.185Z" 13194139534591 true] [17592186078136 1100 "If $D(y)=y\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} - \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} + y^3$, then calculate $D(e^{3x})$." 13194139534591 false] [17592186078136 1100 "If $D(y)=y\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} - \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} + y^3,$ then calculate $D(e^{3x}).$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186078136 1145 "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} +  f_{2}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = y,  f_2 = 0,  f_1 = -1,$ and $f_0 = y^2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y = e^{3x}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{x}) & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({e}^{3x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{3x})+{({e}^{3x})}^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & =27{e}^{6x}-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}({e}^{6x}+27{e}^{3x}-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186078136 1145 "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} + f_{2}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nf_3 = y, f_2 = 0, f_1 = -1\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nf_0 = y^2\n$$\n\nTo compute $D(y)$, we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function\n\n$$\ny = e^{3x}{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD(e^{x}) &= e^{3x}\\frac{d^{3}}{dx^{3}}(e^{3x}) - \\frac{d}{dx}(e^{3x}) + (e^{3x})^{3} \\\\\n&= e^{3x}\\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}}(3e^{3x}) - 3 \\cdot e^{3x} + e^{9x} \\\\\n&= e^{3x}\\frac{d}{dx}(9e^{3x}) - 3 \\cdot e^{3x} + e^{9x} \\\\\n&= 27e^{6x} - 3 \\cdot e^{3x} + e^{9x} \\\\\n&= e^{3x}(e^{6x} + 27e^{3x} - 3)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534591 false] [17592186078256 1100 "Given that $D=\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}}+3 \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}+5$, what is $D(y)$ for $y=e^{-x}$?" 13194139534591 false] [17592186078256 1100 "Given that $D=\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}}+3 \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}+5,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=e^{- x}?$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186078256 1145 "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = a_{2}\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + a_{1}\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + a_0y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients\n\n$$\na_2 = 1, a_1 = 3\n$$\n\nand $a_0 = 5$.\n\nTo compute $D(y)$, we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD(y) &= D(e^{-x}) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}} + 3\\frac{d}{dx} + 5)e^{-x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}}(e^{-x}) + 3\\frac{d}{dx}(e^{-x}) + 5e^{-x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(-e^{-x}) + 3 \\cdot (-e^{-x}) + 5e^{-x} \\\\\n&= e^{-x} - 3e^{-x} + 5e^{-x} \\\\\n&= 3e^{-x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534591 false] [17592186078256 1145 "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = a_{2}\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + a_{1}\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + a_0y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  $a_2 = 1, a_1 = 3,$ and $a_0 = 5.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+5){e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{-x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{-x})+3\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186078257 1100 "Given that $D=x^2\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}}{\\textrm d x^{3}}-5x \\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}} +9\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}$, what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\ln{x}$?" 13194139534591 false] [17592186078257 1100 "Given that $D=x^2\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}}{\\textrm d x^{3}}-5x \\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}} +9\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\ln{x}?$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186078257 1145 "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} + f_{2}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x)y\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nf_3 = x^2, f_2 = -5x, f_1 = 9\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nf_0 = 0\n$$\n\nTo compute $D(y)$, we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD(y) &= D(\\ln x) \\\\\n&= (x^{2}\\frac{d^{3}}{dx^{3}} - 5x\\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}} + 9\\frac{d}{dx})\\ln x \\\\\n&= x^{2}\\frac{d^{3}}{dx^{3}}(\\ln x) - 5x\\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}}(\\ln x) + 9\\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln x) \\\\\n&= x^{2}\\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x}) - 5x\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{1}{x}) + 9 \\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\\n&= x^{2}\\frac{d}{dx}(-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}) - 5x(-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}) + \\frac{9}{x} \\\\\n&= x^{2}(\\frac{2}{x^{3}}) + \\frac{5}{x} + \\frac{9}{x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{x} + \\frac{5}{x} + \\frac{9}{x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{16}{x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534591 false] [17592186078257 1145 "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} + f_{2}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x)y.\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = x^2, f_2 = -5x, f_1 = 9,$ and $f_0 = 0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x})-5x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})+9\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})-5x(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186078505 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297530 13194139534591 true] [17592186078505 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297537 13194139534591 true] [17592186078505 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297544 13194139534591 true] [17592186078505 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297586 13194139534591 true] [17592186078505 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297607 13194139534591 true] [17592186078506 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297551 13194139534591 true] [17592186078506 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297558 13194139534591 true] [17592186078506 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297579 13194139534591 true] [17592186078506 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297593 13194139534591 true] [17592186078506 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297600 13194139534591 true] [17592186078507 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297565 13194139534591 true] [17592186078507 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297572 13194139534591 true] [17592186078786 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534591 true] [17592186078786 1100 "If $D(y) = y\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} - xy\\frac{dy}{dx} + 2y^{2}$, then $D(e^{2x}) =$" 13194139534591 false] [17592186078786 1100 "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-xy\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2},$ then $D({e}^{2x})=$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186078786 1145 "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=y,{f}_{1}=-xy,$ and ${f}_{0}=2y.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={e}^{2x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{2x}) & ={e}^{2x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{2x})-x({e}^{2x})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{2x})+2({e}^{2x})^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{2x})-x{e}^{2x}\\cdot 2{e}^{2x}+2{e}^{4x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot 4{e}^{2x}-2x{e}^{4x}+2{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x}-2x{e}^{4x}+2{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =6{e}^{4x}-2x{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =2{e}^{4x}(3-x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186078787 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534591 true] [17592186078787 1100 "If $D(y) = xy\\frac{d^{3}y}{dx^{3}} + y\\frac{dy}{dx} + 2y$, then $D(x^{3}) =$" 13194139534591 false] [17592186078787 1100 "If $D(y)=xy\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y,$ then $D({x}^{3})=$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186078787 1145 "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=xy,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=y,$ and ${f}_{0}=2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={x}^{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({x}^{3}) & =x({x}^{3})\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({x}^{3})+{x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{x}^{2})+{x}^{3}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)+3{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\cdot 6+3{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & =6{x}^{4}+3{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}(3{x}^{2}+6x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186078788 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534591 true] [17592186078788 1100 "If $D(y) = y\\frac{d^{3}y}{dx^{3}} - xy\\frac{dy}{dx} + 2y$, then $D(\\sin x) =$" 13194139534591 false] [17592186078788 1100 "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-xy\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y,$ then $D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186078788 1145 "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=y,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=-xy,$ and ${f}_{0}=2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(2-(x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186297530 1017 #edb/ref 17592186297531 13194139534591 true] [17592186297530 1089 "q-130083" 13194139534591 true] [17592186297530 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534591 true] [17592186297530 1100 "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={e}^{-2x}+x?$" 13194139534591 true] [17592186297530 1113 #uuid "609ba886-ad8b-5aa8-9b0a-02bc64695179"